I enjoy investigating phishing emails - let's dive into an easy one to see how this platform works.

What is the return path of the email?
Let's go to the top and go to View > Headers > All. And there we see a bunch more information at the top of the email. If we scroll a bit within that, we find:
Return-Path <bounce@rjttznyzjjzydnillquh.designclub.uk.com>

What is the domain name of the url in this mail?
Let's hover over the links in the body of the email. We see that they all start with storage.googleapis.com.

Is the domain mentioned in the previous question suspicious?
If we do a quick search on the domain, we see that storage.googleapis.com is legit, but also frequently used maliciously. So yes, it is suspicious and should at least be worth looking into.

What is the body SHA-256 of the domain?
Let's plug in "storage.googleapis.com" into VirusTotal and we get: 13945ecc33afee74ac7f72e1d5bb73050894356c4bf63d02a1a53e76830567f5

Is this email a phishing email?
Yeah, probably. It looks sketchy even before you go digging, and investigation sure didn't help its case.
